Just give me a second.

251
00:14:11,460 --> 00:14:12,297
He'll be good and dead.

252
00:14:12,380 --> 00:14:13,210
No way

253
00:14:21,980 --> 00:14:25,280
A new order, and it's true.

254
00:14:25,640 --> 00:14:28,600
He really does want me dead.

255
00:14:29,620 --> 00:14:31,140
Screw this crap.

256
00:14:34,520 --> 00:14:36,320
And screw you two!

257
00:14:39,160 --> 00:14:40,920
Get out of my way!

258
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:45,600
Let me kill him.

259
00:14:45,960 --> 00:14:48,080
I am going to stop him dead.

260
00:14:48,380 --> 00:14:49,760
Now, move!

261
00:14:50,880 --> 00:14:51,710
You kidding?

262
00:14:51,920 --> 00:14:53,740
I'm not budging an inch.

263
00:14:54,240 --> 00:14:56,677
You don't want your boss
getting mad, do you?

264
00:14:56,760 --> 00:14:58,300
So just go already!

265
00:15:00,120 --> 00:15:02,238
You and your barrier can go to hell!

266
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:04,264
This isn't over by a long shot!

267
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:08,040
Mark my words, you're not
leaving Dressrosa alive!

268
00:15:10,260 --> 00:15:12,436
Yeah, yeah, that's what they all say.

269
00:15:13,940 --> 00:15:17,020
That was Diamante on
the transponder snail.

270
00:15:17,860 --> 00:15:20,257
So everything Della just said was true.

271
00:15:20,340 --> 00:15:24,957
That means Doflamingo was the
one who was lying all this time.

272
00:15:25,040 --> 00:15:29,037
He was toying with me, so I
just gotta win the tournament,

273
00:15:29,120 --> 00:15:31,900
then you'll give me a spot in the family!

274
00:15:33,420 --> 00:15:34,540
Of course.

275
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:39,280
I'll be cheering for you.

276
00:15:39,600 --> 00:15:41,180
Good luck out there

277
00:15:42,560 --> 00:15:45,860
Let me take you to the
medical world, buddy. Damn it!

278
00:15:46,100 --> 00:15:47,557
I don't need you butting it!

279
00:15:47,640 --> 00:15:48,480
Just go away!

280
00:15:48,800 --> 00:15:49,820
Leave me alone!

281
00:15:50,560 --> 00:15:52,720
I've lost my only reason to live!

282
00:15:53,300 --> 00:15:56,829
Why the hell do you want to
save me in the first place, huh?

283
00:15:57,200 --> 00:15:58,580
We were enemies!

284
00:15:59,580 --> 00:16:03,756
I would have killed you along with
everyone else in that battle royale!

285
00:16:03,960 --> 00:16:06,380
Now you're protecting me! Yep.

286
00:16:08,020 --> 00:16:09,785
We may fight in the same ring.

287
00:16:09,920 --> 00:16:11,097
They become like brothers.

288
00:16:11,180 --> 00:16:12,886
We're comrades in battle now.

289
00:16:15,840 --> 00:16:19,340
And dammit, I'd never
turn my back on a comrade.

290
00:16:26,620 --> 00:16:29,267
Now you know the dark
history of this nation.

291
00:16:30,480 --> 00:16:35,060
And next, I shall tell you how
I plan to liberate its people.

292
00:16:35,520 --> 00:16:37,580
What do I call this plan, you ask?

293
00:16:39,860 --> 00:16:41,600
Operation Dressrosa S .O .P.

294
00:16:44,700 --> 00:16:46,480
S .O .P., huh?

295
00:16:46,780 --> 00:16:48,427
So what does that stand for?

296
00:16:48,940 --> 00:16:52,528
Beneath this kingdom, there is
a massive underground network.

297
00:16:53,200 --> 00:16:54,917
Unbeknownst to the people above,

298
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:59,882
there lies a trade port for black market
dealings, as well as a mysterious factory.

299
00:17:00,100 --> 00:17:01,637
There, the captured Tontara,

300
00:17:01,720 --> 00:17:04,477
along with the humans who have
been transformed into toys,

301
00:17:04,560 --> 00:17:06,157
are forced to work around the clock.

302
00:17:06,240 --> 00:17:07,260
Okay, cool.

303
00:17:07,560 --> 00:17:09,520
But what does SLP mean again?

304
00:17:09,880 --> 00:17:11,797
We'll sneak in through
an underground passage

305
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:14,217
that we've been digging
for an entire year.

306
00:17:14,300 --> 00:17:16,240
Then, we'll rescue everyone.

307
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:18,028
We'll wreck the facilities.

308
00:17:18,540 --> 00:17:20,700
And defeat the Doflamingo family.

309
00:17:20,980 --> 00:17:23,451
Then, King Rick will return to the throne.

310
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:26,400
That is the goal of our operation.

311
00:17:26,600 --> 00:17:28,477
I doubt it'll be quite that easy.

312
00:17:28,560 --> 00:17:30,736
Of course there may be complications.

313
00:17:31,420 --> 00:17:34,897
After all, none of us can predict
what might happen in Dres Rosa.

314
00:17:34,980 --> 00:17:36,862
especially in its current state.

315
00:17:39,240 --> 00:17:43,780
That said, there is one thing
we must do if we want to win.

316
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:50,280
The one who turned us into toys is a
member of Doflamingo's inner circle.

317
00:17:50,960 --> 00:17:55,019
We'll target them and shut down the
power of their Hobby Hobby fruit.

318
00:17:55,980 --> 00:17:57,260
Hobby Hobby what?

319
00:17:57,860 --> 00:17:59,840
We simply have to knock them out.

320
00:18:00,900 --> 00:18:03,397
And doing so will break
the spell on the toys?

321
00:18:03,480 --> 00:18:04,362
That's correct.

322
00:18:04,800 --> 00:18:07,677
All of the toys will return
to their human forms,

323
00:18:07,760 --> 00:18:10,348
in the secret factory
and the streets alike.

324
00:18:11,420 --> 00:18:15,891
Then, the lost memories of them will
come flooding back to their loved ones.

325
00:18:16,440 --> 00:18:20,357
While that's a victory in itself,
it's hard to say what will follow.

326
00:18:20,440 --> 00:18:23,820
How many of the former toys
will rise up in arms with us?

327
00:18:24,140 --> 00:18:26,417
What will the citizens
think when their memories

328
00:18:26,500 --> 00:18:29,088
are restored and what
action will they take?

329
00:18:29,480 --> 00:18:31,480
How will Dol Flamingo respond?

330
00:18:31,720 --> 00:18:33,249
How will the Navy respond?

331
00:18:34,220 --> 00:18:35,977
The only thing that we know for certain is

332
00:18:36,060 --> 00:18:38,589
that the kingdom will
be thrown into chaos.

333
00:18:38,960 --> 00:18:42,817
So this person with the hobby hobby
power, the one who changed everybody,

334
00:18:42,900 --> 00:18:44,120
where are they now?

335
00:18:44,320 --> 00:18:46,202
They must be pretty strong, huh?

336
00:18:46,820 --> 00:18:49,097
According to our Tontara scouting unit,

337
00:18:49,180 --> 00:18:52,886
she should be in the underground
trade port for the time being.

338
00:18:54,520 --> 00:18:57,140
She's a special officer
in the Treble Army.

339
00:18:58,140 --> 00:18:59,700
Her name is Sugar.

340
00:19:03,020 --> 00:19:07,740
She is a girl who can transform anything
into a toy simply by touching it.

341
00:19:07,900 --> 00:19:09,429
She appears to be a child,

342
00:19:09,540 --> 00:19:11,697
but it seems that anyone
who eats the Hobby Hobby

343
00:19:11,780 --> 00:19:14,757
Fruit stops aging the moment
that its power takes hold.

344
00:19:14,840 --> 00:19:16,722
Since she's such a vital figure,

345
00:19:16,980 --> 00:19:19,157
she is under the constant
protection of Treble,

346
00:19:19,240 --> 00:19:22,100
one of Doflamingo's
highest officers. I see,

347
00:19:22,260 --> 00:19:26,357
but we can avoid a conflict with Treble
just as long as we can knock out sugar.

348
00:19:26,440 --> 00:19:27,600
That's correct.

349
00:19:27,900 --> 00:19:31,606
The plan is to scare her out of
her wits and make her pass out.

350
00:19:32,360 --> 00:19:35,660
Operation Sugar Oversurprised Bannock!

351
00:19:37,300 --> 00:19:41,740
And that is the meaning behind
SOP, my inquisitive friend. Ow!

352
00:19:42,100 --> 00:19:45,041
Now that's the kind of
name I can get behind, bro!

353
00:19:45,220 --> 00:19:47,657
If it's a little girl
we're fighting, no problem!

354
00:19:47,740 --> 00:19:48,570
Follow me!

355
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:53,620
Alright, I'm getting all fired up.

356
00:19:54,380 --> 00:19:56,145
Franky Aresolat in the house!

357
00:19:57,560 --> 00:19:59,900
You dick my combat hair!

358
00:20:01,160 --> 00:20:02,597
Yay, Fraland!

359
00:20:02,680 --> 00:20:03,700
Yay, Usaland!

360
00:20:04,400 --> 00:20:06,740
You guys are the best! Aw, yeah!

361
00:20:07,120 --> 00:20:08,757
Usaland is gonna save the day!

362
00:20:08,840 --> 00:20:11,860
Ain't no plan too grand for Fraland! Wow!

363
00:20:12,500 --> 00:20:16,676
Now take us to the underground, little
dudes, cause we are ready to go!

364
00:20:16,820 --> 00:20:19,080
Yeah, Usaland guys!

365
00:20:23,320 --> 00:20:24,150
Meanwhile,

366
00:20:24,260 --> 00:20:26,517
Luffy runs from one passage to the next,

367
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:30,129
frantically searching for the
exit to the Corridor Coliseum.

368
00:20:34,320 --> 00:20:35,280
Hold on.

369
00:20:35,800 --> 00:20:37,200
Forget the exit.

370
00:20:38,060 --> 00:20:39,480
Where am I?

371
00:20:39,720 --> 00:20:43,000
So the plan is, someday,
I'm going to be Mr.

372
00:20:43,140 --> 00:20:44,258
Luffy's apprentice.

373
00:20:44,900 --> 00:20:46,840
Well, it's more like my dream.

374
00:20:50,480 --> 00:20:52,020
Oh, the bathroom!

375
00:20:52,620 --> 00:20:53,450
Huh?

376
00:20:56,040 --> 00:20:57,280
Roosterhood, it's me!

377
00:20:57,680 --> 00:21:00,220
And am I glad to see you! Ah!

378
00:21:01,220 --> 00:21:03,520
M-m-mister Luffy!

379
00:21:10,480 --> 00:21:13,037
Pull it together, Baratie! Mr.

380
00:21:13,120 --> 00:21:15,137
Luffy's gonna be the king of the pirates!

381
00:21:15,220 --> 00:21:17,657
You gotta make a better
impression than this!

382
00:21:17,740 --> 00:21:18,880
Oh, it's Bellamy!

383
00:21:24,140 --> 00:21:25,217
He's too radiant.

384
00:21:25,300 --> 00:21:27,120
It's like staring at the sun.

385
00:21:27,800 --> 00:21:29,140
Hey, Mr. Luffy.

386
00:21:29,560 --> 00:21:31,480
I don't remember what happened.

387
00:21:31,800 --> 00:21:32,877
Did you get to see Mr.

388
00:21:32,960 --> 00:21:33,790
Zoro?

389
00:21:33,873 --> 00:21:34,703
Yeah, I sure did.

390
00:21:34,786 --> 00:21:35,936
Thanks for the help.

391
00:21:36,240 --> 00:21:37,540
It was my pleasure.

392
00:21:37,920 --> 00:21:40,317
Anyway, I gotta get somewhere quick, see?

393
00:21:40,400 --> 00:21:41,929
But I can't find the exit.

394
00:21:42,320 --> 00:21:43,377
Think you can help again?

395
00:21:43,460 --> 00:21:44,740
There is no exit.

396
00:21:45,060 --> 00:21:46,940
You have to keep on fighting.

397
00:21:48,460 --> 00:21:49,640
Hold on. Bellamy?

398
00:21:50,020 --> 00:21:51,580
Why are you so beat up?

399
00:21:52,300 --> 00:21:53,500
Never mind that.

400
00:21:53,920 --> 00:21:57,937
I'm telling you, there's no escape from
this place unless they want you to leave.

401
00:21:58,020 --> 00:22:00,497
You might as well stop
looking and give up hope.

402
00:22:00,580 --> 00:22:02,120
There's no way out. How?

403
00:22:02,320 --> 00:22:03,438
There was a way in.

404
00:22:03,600 --> 00:22:04,660
It's an emergency.

405
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:08,760
You work for Doflamingo, right? Come on.

406
00:22:09,440 --> 00:22:11,960
Please, you gotta know a secret way out.

407
00:22:12,360 --> 00:22:13,980
You work for Doflamingo?

408
00:22:14,200 --> 00:22:16,680
I wasn't even good enough to be as flunky.

409
00:22:17,720 --> 00:22:18,550
Bellamy!

410
00:22:18,633 --> 00:22:20,300
My friends need my help!

411
00:22:20,540 --> 00:22:23,128
I'm looking to get out
of this place myself.

412
00:22:23,620 --> 00:22:26,180
If you follow me, maybe
you'll get out too.

413
00:22:26,480 --> 00:22:27,680
But no promises!

414
00:22:28,680 --> 00:22:30,160
Really? Thanks, buddy!

415
00:22:30,540 --> 00:22:32,077
Glad you're showing me the way!

416
00:22:32,160 --> 00:22:34,101
I'm not showing you a damn thing!

417
00:22:34,380 --> 00:22:36,380
I just won't stop you, that's all!

418
00:22:38,240 --> 00:22:41,122
You're not telling me to
betray my boss, are you?

419
00:22:42,600 --> 00:22:43,640
Even now...

420
00:22:44,460 --> 00:22:45,940
I'm loyal to Doflamingo!

421
00:22:47,380 --> 00:22:52,757
No matter what I'll always respect him,
come on, man, just a second ago, you?

422
00:22:52,840 --> 00:22:53,670
I don't care.

423
00:22:53,753 --> 00:22:55,837
I've got my own honor to uphold.

424
00:22:55,920 --> 00:22:56,997
That's fine.

425
00:22:57,080 --> 00:22:58,500
I'll follow you out.

426
00:23:00,120 --> 00:23:02,940
but wait what about the
flame flame fruit mr.

427
00:23:03,040 --> 00:23:06,137
Luffy there's one guy I hope
doesn't win but it's fine.

428
00:23:06,220 --> 00:23:08,537
the lives of my friends matter way more.

429
00:23:08,620 --> 00:23:09,497
don't worry!

430
00:23:09,580 --> 00:23:11,077
I'll take care of that for you.

431
00:23:11,160 --> 00:23:13,817
in fact, that was my plan
from the very start of.

432
00:23:13,900 --> 00:23:17,157
I knew you'd want a keepsake
from your dear departed brother,

433
00:23:17,240 --> 00:23:19,217
so I was going to win it
and then give it to you.

434
00:23:19,300 --> 00:23:20,130
Really?

435
00:23:20,213 --> 00:23:21,043
Do you mean it?

436
00:23:21,126 --> 00:23:21,956
Of course!

437
00:23:22,120 --> 00:23:23,340
It was destinable.

438
00:23:24,340 --> 00:23:26,840
Uh, you're getting hard to understand.

439
00:23:27,600 --> 00:23:29,365
Don't you worry about nothing.

440
00:23:29,480 --> 00:23:33,677
Just go and save the day and let old
Bartle take care of the tournament for you.

441
00:23:33,760 --> 00:23:35,437
Why are you telling that to the wall?

442
00:23:35,520 --> 00:23:36,350
Thanks!

443
00:23:36,433 --> 00:23:37,434
You're awesome, buddy.

444
00:23:37,540 --> 00:23:41,305
If you think you're getting the
flame flame fruit, you're wrong.

445
00:23:43,900 --> 00:23:45,720
Sorry, Luffy. It's mine.

446
00:23:47,800 --> 00:23:50,620
Oh, yeah? You want to fight? Listen up!

447
00:23:50,920 --> 00:23:53,917
I don't know who the hell you
think you are, but that's Mr.

448
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:55,647
Luffy to you, you damn punk!

449
00:23:56,040 --> 00:23:59,057
The Flame Flame Fruit belonged
to his brother, Firefist Ace,

450
00:23:59,140 --> 00:24:01,397
so nobody deserves to
have it more than him.

451
00:24:01,480 --> 00:24:05,245
Also, he's going to be King of
the Pirates one day, you jackass!

452
00:24:05,340 --> 00:24:06,170
I know.

453
00:24:06,253 --> 00:24:07,769
I've known that for years.

454
00:24:17,580 --> 00:24:20,180
You're facing the moment of truth now.

455
00:24:21,080 --> 00:24:23,800
Rebecca, you get to
the finals at any cost.

456
00:24:26,160 --> 00:24:26,990
Right.

457
00:24:40,600 --> 00:24:42,577
This moron's pissing me off.

458
00:24:42,660 --> 00:24:44,260
He got a grudge against Mr.

459
00:24:44,360 --> 00:24:45,190
Luffy or what?

460
00:24:45,600 --> 00:24:47,776
Look, you're upsetting him, you jerk!

461
00:25:05,180 --> 00:25:06,010
Luffy?

462
00:25:17,360 --> 00:25:19,280
You got out of the damn place.

463
00:25:19,480 --> 00:25:20,598
Why are you crying?

464
00:25:21,560 --> 00:25:24,077
What do you mean you can't
find the pirate hunter?

465
00:25:24,160 --> 00:25:25,219
He was right here.

466
00:25:25,400 --> 00:25:26,477
Call the vice-admiral.

467
00:25:26,560 --> 00:25:27,820
Hurry. Yes, sir.

468
00:25:31,260 --> 00:25:33,657
It seems my flawless disguises have fooled

469
00:25:33,740 --> 00:25:36,077
the Navy into thinking we're not but toys.

470
00:25:36,160 --> 00:25:37,360
Flawless, my ass.

471
00:25:37,520 --> 00:25:39,057
Look how much we stick out.

472
00:25:39,140 --> 00:25:40,611
These costumes are weird.

473
00:25:41,320 --> 00:25:44,000
But I chose all the
best animals, like carp.

474
00:25:44,400 --> 00:25:45,282
Carp are great.

475
00:25:48,640 --> 00:25:50,100
Stop crying already.

476
00:25:50,320 --> 00:25:52,144
You want to save Traffy or not?

477
00:25:53,060 --> 00:25:54,620
I'll save Traffy.

478
00:25:54,860 --> 00:25:56,680
And I'll kick Mango's ass.

479
00:25:56,980 --> 00:26:00,215
Now I know the Flame Flame
Fruit will be in good hands.

480
00:26:00,300 --> 00:26:01,476
What does that mean?

481
00:26:01,980 --> 00:26:04,340
I heard Robin's in Dressrosa, too.

482
00:26:04,720 --> 00:26:06,014
Oh, it's been forever.

483
00:26:06,400 --> 00:26:07,437
Hope I can see her.

484
00:26:07,520 --> 00:26:09,285
I'm glad you got to see Luffy.

485
00:26:10,640 --> 00:26:13,228
Yeah, I was afraid he
was going to punch me.

486
00:26:16,240 --> 00:26:18,040
Are you crying? What?

487
00:26:18,260 --> 00:26:19,200
I don't cry.

488
00:26:22,140 --> 00:26:24,297
You're wondering if you
could have saved him.

489
00:26:24,380 --> 00:26:25,792
If you'd been there too?

490
00:26:30,920 --> 00:26:34,217
Let me know as soon as you have
more info on this underground place.

491
00:26:34,300 --> 00:26:35,130
Okay.

492
00:26:37,520 --> 00:26:38,579
In the meantime...

493
00:26:39,300 --> 00:26:41,888
I'll be taking back
that fruit for you, Ace.

494
00:26:46,160 --> 00:26:49,340
Luffy and I will carry on your will.

495
00:26:52,940 --> 00:26:55,840
I never thought he might still be alive.

496
00:26:56,040 --> 00:26:58,099
Who the hell are you talking about?

497
00:27:00,280 --> 00:27:02,180
I was sure he died.

498
00:27:03,660 --> 00:27:05,260
Almost years ago.

499
00:27:05,560 --> 00:27:06,720
He was out there.

500
00:27:14,660 --> 00:27:16,072
Thank you for listening.
